project: Task tests blocked: Acceptance command 3 is unsatisfiable as written, independent of my changes. Its command substitution `$(git -C . rev-parse --show-toplevel)` is expanded after `cd "$(dirname "$d")"` has left the repository, so git exits 128 (the exact error the harness reported) and npm is run with an empty `--prefix`, exiting 254 with ENOENT on the temp dir's package.json. Since the empty prefix means npm never reads this project's package.json, nothing I can change in test/** or package.json can make the command exit 0; only reordering the acceptance command (capturing the repo root before the cd) fixes it, and that reordered command already exits 0 and runs all 18 tests. The task deliverable itself is complete, but I cannot make this acceptance command pass without either editing the acceptance command or gaming the check from outside my file scope..
